-- int-tests-wiring: the integration points one by one, each run through the integration layer's wiring and asserted against the Law.  Where a test is also in another module (IP19 to IP24, IP27, IP28, IP32, IP34 in the
-- scenarios of headlines (a), (b), (c) and (f)) it is not repeated; this module covers IP6, IP11, IP15 and IP16, IP25, IP26, IP29, IP31 and the PLAN's "forks that must be set together".
-- EXPECTED VALUES were decided by hand from the Law before this module was run.

§ `Integration layer -- the standard inputs, one by one`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
fleet MEANS `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`

§§ `IP6 -- the entity is a registered charity: group G1's Article 1 against the register's stored standing`

-- For a company in each standing the register can record, G1 (which needs an entity under Article 2(1)) and the standing alone (the section named by it) agree: registered exactly in the general and restricted sections.
GIVEN standing IS A `Standing on the register` @desc The standing
GIVETH AN Entity
`the school company with the standing` standing MEANS
    `Int IP5 the entity` fleet `the text of 2 October 2026` EMPTY (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Body in the case` WITH name IS "Gorey Schools Limited", standing IS standing, purposes IS ((`Int fx the registered school company`)'s purposes), facts IS ((`Int fx the registered school company`)'s facts), model IS `Int fx clear model facts`, people IS EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` (`the school company with the standing` `not on the register`)
#ASSERT NOT `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` (`the school company with the standing` `an applicant for registration`)
#ASSERT `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` (`the school company with the standing` `entered in the general section`)
#ASSERT `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` (`the school company with the standing` `entered in the restricted section`)
#ASSERT NOT `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` (`the school company with the standing` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`)

§§ `IP11 with F2.5 and F8.3 -- the forks that must be set together: a humanist association and "organized religious charity"`

-- A purpose of advancing a philosophical belief (whether or not involving belief in a god) is, by Article 6(2)(f), "analogous to" the advancement of religion for the purposes of paragraph (1)(p). So it falls within (p), not (c) (F2.5,
-- reading taken). Article 28(1)(a) allows an Order to categorize charities that meet the charity test "by virtue of Article 6(1)(c)". Whether a humanist association can be so categorized is decided by TWO forks, one in G2 (does
-- the purpose fall within (c)?) and one in G8 (does 28(1)(a) reach an analogous purpose?). Either fork on its other reading makes it eligible; on the readings taken it is not.
GIVETH A Purpose
`a purpose of advancing humanism` MEANS
    Purpose WITH description IS "to advance humanism", head IS JUST `any other purpose that may reasonably be regarded as analogous to one of the above`, `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE, `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE, `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS TRUE

GIVETH AN Entity
`the humanist association` MEANS
    `Entity` WITH name IS "Jersey Humanists", `standing on the register` IS `entered in the general section`, `kinds of entity` IS (LIST `a company`), `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE, governors IS EMPTY, purposes IS (LIST `a purpose of advancing humanism`)

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
`the readings with F2.5 read as B` MEANS `Int fx the readings with the reading of Articles 3 to 7` fleet `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.5 read as B`
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36`
g8A MEANS `the favoured interpretation`
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36`
g8B MEANS `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.3`

#ASSERT NOT `Int IP11 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` fleet `the humanist association`
#ASSERT `Int IP11 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` `the readings with F2.5 read as B` `the humanist association`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 28(1)(a) the charity meets the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c)` g8A TRUE (`Int IP11 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` fleet `the humanist association`) `the humanist association`
#ASSERT `Art 28(1)(a) the charity meets the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c)` g8A TRUE (`Int IP11 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` `the readings with F2.5 read as B` `the humanist association`) `the humanist association`
#ASSERT `Art 28(1)(a) the charity meets the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c)` g8B TRUE (`Int IP11 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` fleet `the humanist association`) `the humanist association`
#ASSERT `Art 28(1)(a) the charity meets the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c)` g8B TRUE (`Int IP11 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` `the readings with F2.5 read as B` `the humanist association`) `the humanist association`

§§ `IP15 and IP16 with F8.14 -- a registered charity that has ceased to meet Article 11(4)(d): the principal address from group G3 reaches group G8's Article 27(1)(e)`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Belief that prompts a required steps notice`
`the Commissioner believes the charity has ceased to meet Article 11(4)` MEANS LIST `a registered charity has ceased to meet the requirements of Article 11(4)(c) or (d)`
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36`
g8C MEANS `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.14`

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of group G8
      address IS A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` @desc The facts Article 8(4) reads
GIVETH A LIST OF `Belief that prompts a required steps notice`
`the grounds of a charity whose Commissioner believes it has ceased to meet Article 11(4)` interp address MEANS
    `Art 27(1) the Commissioner has a ground to serve a required steps notice` interp TRUE `the Commissioner believes the charity has ceased to meet Article 11(4)` FALSE TRUE FALSE entity FALSE ip15 ip16
    WHERE
        entity MEANS `the school company with the standing` `entered in the general section`
        ip15 MEANS `Art 11(4)(c) the requirement is met` entity TRUE TRUE
        ip16 MEANS `Art 11(4)(d) the requirement is met` (`Int IP17 the entity has a principal address in Jersey` fleet entity address)

-- Taken (F8.14, belief alone is the ground): the belief is a ground whatever the facts.
#ASSERT `the grounds of a charity whose Commissioner believes it has ceased to meet Article 11(4)` g8A (`Int fx a registered office in Jersey at` "1 Esplanade, St Helier") EQUALS `the Commissioner believes the charity has ceased to meet Article 11(4)`
#ASSERT `the grounds of a charity whose Commissioner believes it has ceased to meet Article 11(4)` g8A `Int fx no address in Jersey` EQUALS `the Commissioner believes the charity has ceased to meet Article 11(4)`
-- Other reading (the belief must be borne out): with a registered office in Jersey, requirement (d) is met, so the belief is not borne out; without any address in Jersey it is.
#ASSERT `the grounds of a charity whose Commissioner believes it has ceased to meet Article 11(4)` g8C (`Int fx a registered office in Jersey at` "1 Esplanade, St Helier") EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the grounds of a charity whose Commissioner believes it has ceased to meet Article 11(4)` g8C `Int fx no address in Jersey` EQUALS `the Commissioner believes the charity has ceased to meet Article 11(4)`

§§ `IP17 -- an applicant with no principal address in Jersey fails Article 11(4)(d): the Commissioner must refuse`

-- No registered office is required of this applicant's constitutional Law and there is no main premises or governor's address in Jersey: Article 8(4) gives no principal address, so Article 11(4)(d) is not met.
GIVETH A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))`
`the facts of a company whose constitutional Law requires a Jersey registered office that it lacks` MEANS
    `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` WITH `its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey` IS FALSE, `registered office or business address in Jersey` IS NOTHING, `main premises in Jersey from which its activities in Jersey are managed, controlled or undertaken` IS NOTHING, `addresses in Jersey of the governors` IS EMPTY
GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the school application` MEANS
    `Application in the case` WITH
        body IS `Int fx the registered school company`
        `charity test facts` IS `Int fx the charity test facts with` `Int fx a determination that public benefit is provided`
        application IS `Int fx a complete application lodged on` (YMD 2026 6 1)
        findings IS `Int fx clear findings`
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the principal address` IS `Int fx a registered office in Jersey at` "1 Esplanade, St Helier"
        `opinion on the name` IS `Int fx a name with no objection` "Gorey Schools Limited"
        `the application states that the entity holds declarations` IS TRUE
        `orders of the court` IS EMPTY
        `notices served` IS EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Int fx the application with facts for the principal address replaced` `the school application` `the facts of a company whose constitutional Law requires a Jersey registered office that it lacks`))'s `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Int fx the application with facts for the principal address replaced` `the school application` `the facts of a company whose constitutional Law requires a Jersey registered office that it lacks`))'s duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the school application`)'s `the application may be granted`

§§ `IP29 -- an Order under Article 13(9) that requires only payment details (limb (a)): group G5's composite fact is TRUE, group G4 reads limb (b)`

GIVETH A `Order under Article 13(9)`
`an Order that requires payment details in the annual return only` MEANS
    `Order under Article 13(9)` WITH `requires details of prescribed payments in the annual return, Article 13(9)(a)` IS TRUE, `requires a statement of current intentions as to such payments, Article 13(9)(b)` IS FALSE, `provides for entry on the register, Article 13(9)(c)` IS FALSE
-- Article 11(2)(e)(ii) asks for a draft statement of intentions only "if an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies". An Order of limb (a) alone does not, so an application without a draft statement is complete; wired from G5's
-- composite fact it would be incomplete.
#ASSERT `Int IP29 the composite fact of group G5` fleet (JUST `an Order that requires payment details in the annual return only`) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Int IP29 an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies` fleet (JUST `an Order that requires payment details in the annual return only`) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Int IP29 an Order under Article 13(9)(c) applies` fleet (JUST `an Order that requires payment details in the annual return only`) EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 11 and 12`) ((`the school application`)'s application) (`Int IP29 an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies` fleet (JUST `an Order that requires payment details in the annual return only`) EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 11 and 12`) ((`the school application`)'s application) (`Int IP29 the composite fact of group G5` fleet (JUST `an Order that requires payment details in the annual return only`) EMPTY)
-- An Order of limb (b) applies to the applicant as it would be once registered, so the draft statement is needed.
GIVETH A `Order under Article 13(9)`
`an Order that requires a statement of intentions` MEANS
    `Order under Article 13(9)` WITH `requires details of prescribed payments in the annual return, Article 13(9)(a)` IS FALSE, `requires a statement of current intentions as to such payments, Article 13(9)(b)` IS TRUE, `provides for entry on the register, Article 13(9)(c)` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `Int IP29 an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies` fleet (JUST `an Order that requires a statement of intentions`) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 11 and 12`) ((`the school application`)'s application) (`Int IP29 an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies` fleet (JUST `an Order that requires a statement of intentions`) EMPTY)

§§ `IP25 -- the information registered in a public part of the register (group G3, Article 10(3)) reaches group G8's offence of Article 29(1)`

GIVETH AN `Information received and its character`
`information about a charity's affairs received under the Law` MEANS
    `Information received and its character` WITH `relates to the business or other affairs of a person` IS TRUE, `received under or for the purposes of this Law` IS TRUE, `received directly or indirectly from a person who so received it` IS FALSE, `already made available to the public from other sources` IS FALSE, `in the form of a summary or collection that identifies no particular person` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Disclosure of information`
`a disclosure to any other person, without consent` MEANS
    `Disclosure of information` WITH `by or on behalf of the Commissioner` IS FALSE, recipient IS `a disclosure to any other person`, `to enable the Commissioner to discharge a function` IS FALSE, `to enable the recipient to discharge a function` IS FALSE, `to enable the recipient to discharge a function in relation to charities` IS FALSE, `for the investigation or prosecution of an offence` IS FALSE, `for taking or deciding whether to take proceedings under this Law` IS FALSE, `in circumstances prescribed by Regulations` IS FALSE, `required by the recipient for its functions` IS FALSE, `consent of the person to whom the information relates` IS FALSE, `consent of the person from whom the information was received` IS FALSE
-- The registered name of a charity in the general section is in a public part of the register (Article 10(3)(a)): Article 29 does not apply to it, so disclosing it is not an offence.
GIVETH AN `Act alleged in the case`
`disclosing the registered name of a general section charity` MEANS
    `disclosing restricted information under Article 29` WITH body IS `Int fx the registered school company`, matter IS `the registered name`, `the Commissioner has designated the matter as not a public part of the register` IS FALSE, info IS `information about a charity's affairs received under the Law`, disclosure IS `a disclosure to any other person, without consent`
-- The Commissioner has designated that matter as not public (Article 10(5)), because of a risk to safety (Article 10(4)): it is not in a public part, so the disclosure without consent is an offence: 24 months and a fine.
GIVETH AN `Act alleged in the case`
`disclosing a registered name the Commissioner designated as not public` MEANS
    `disclosing restricted information under Article 29` WITH body IS `Int fx the registered school company`, matter IS `the registered name`, `the Commissioner has designated the matter as not a public part of the register` IS TRUE, info IS `information about a charity's affairs received under the Law`, disclosure IS `a disclosure to any other person, without consent`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `disclosing the registered name of a general section charity`, officer IS NOTHING))'s `an offence is made out`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `disclosing a registered name the Commissioner designated as not public`, officer IS NOTHING))'s `an offence is made out`
-- Trap T16, reading taken (F3.3): the historic section's matters are public, and a designation under 10(4) reaches only a "registered charity" (general or restricted section): for a formerly registered entity the designation has no effect,
-- so the matter stays public and the disclosure is no offence.
GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`the deregistered school company` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH name IS "Gorey Schools Limited", standing IS `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`, purposes IS ((`Int fx the registered school company`)'s purposes), facts IS ((`Int fx the registered school company`)'s facts), model IS `Int fx clear model facts`, people IS EMPTY
GIVETH AN `Act alleged in the case`
`disclosing a historic section matter the Commissioner designated as not public` MEANS
    `disclosing restricted information under Article 29` WITH body IS `the deregistered school company`, matter IS `the registered name`, `the Commissioner has designated the matter as not a public part of the register` IS TRUE, info IS `information about a charity's affairs received under the Law`, disclosure IS `a disclosure to any other person, without consent`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `disclosing a historic section matter the Commissioner designated as not public`, officer IS NOTHING))'s `an offence is made out`

§§ `IP26 -- an excepted foreign charity (group G7, Article 22) and the prohibition of Article 21(5)`

-- An entity established under the law of the United Kingdom, entitled there to call itself a charity and managed from there, is an excepted foreign charity (Article 22): Article 21(5), which binds an entity that is
-- NEITHER a Jersey entity NOR an excepted foreign charity, does not bind it. An otherwise identical entity established under the law of some other jurisdiction (not prescribed by Order) is not excepted, and 21(5) does.
GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`a foreign body not registered in Jersey` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH name IS "Normandie Aid SARL", standing IS `not on the register`, purposes IS ((`Int fx the registered school company`)'s purposes), facts IS `Int fx a foreign body similar to` (LIST `a company`), model IS `Int fx clear model facts`, people IS EMPTY
GIVEN law IS A `Law under which an entity is established` @desc The law
GIVETH A `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test`
`the facts of a foreign body established under` law MEANS
    `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` WITH `established under` IS law, `entitled under that law to refer to itself there as a charity` IS TRUE, `managed wholly or mainly from that jurisdiction` IS TRUE, `specified in an Order under Article 22(4)` IS FALSE
GIVEN exceptedFacts IS A `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` @desc The facts for Article 22
GIVETH AN `Act alleged in the case`
`the foreign body calls itself a charity in connection with its Jersey activities, facts` exceptedFacts MEANS
    `a statement about an entity` WITH body IS `a foreign body not registered in Jersey`, `facts for the excepted foreign charity test` IS exceptedFacts, `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS FALSE, statement IS `Int fx a statement by the entity itself saying` `that it is a “charity”`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the foreign body calls itself a charity in connection with its Jersey activities, facts` (`the facts of a foreign body established under` `the law of the United Kingdom or of a jurisdiction that is part of the United Kingdom`), officer IS NOTHING))'s `an offence is made out`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the foreign body calls itself a charity in connection with its Jersey activities, facts` (`the facts of a foreign body established under` `the law of some other jurisdiction`), officer IS NOTHING))'s penalties EQUALS LIST (`Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS NOTHING, fine IS `a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3)
